# Both GitHub Environments: staging and production. docs/GITHUB-ENVIRONMENTS.md
# Required SECRETS (7), plus 2 private support settings:
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY
# DATABASE_URL
# RESEND_API_KEY
# INTERNAL_DEPLOY_TOKEN
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY (web only; staging may be empty until configured)
# RESEND_WEBHOOK_SECRET (web only; staging may be empty until configured)
# RESTIC_PASSWORD
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY
# Required VARIABLES (9):
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL
# NEXT_PUBLIC_REALTIME_URL
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY
# MAIL_FROM
# MAIL_REPLY_TO
# RESTIC_REPOSITORY
# AWS_DEFAULT_REGION
# Optional VARIABLES:
# LANDING_ORIGIN
# SUPPORT_INBOUND_ADDRESS=support@ontvangen.dartspoint.nl
# SUPPORT_RESEND_DOMAIN_ID (domain matching MAIL_FROM, open/click tracking both off)
# GOOGLE_AUTH_ENABLED=false (enable only after provider configuration)
# DATABASE_CA_CERT_BASE64
# NODE_IMAGE, REDIS_IMAGE, POSTGRES_IMAGE, CLAMAV_IMAGE: only ops/image-pins.json, not Environment vars.
# AWS_* credentials come from Hetzner S3, not Amazon AWS.
# RESTIC_PASSWORD: create for new repository and keep in password vault.
# OTP SMTP and Auth CAPTCHA remain in Supabase; support Turnstile also needs the web-only secret above.
# Production requires both private support secrets and configured support receiving/sending identifiers.
# Owner UUID/email/confirmation: temporary private operator config, never automatic deployment.

# Optional in BOTH environments until AI is configured. Web and npc service only.
# SECRET AI_INTEGRATION_MASTER_KEY_B64: canonical base64 of 32 random bytes
# VARIABLE AI_INTEGRATION_MASTER_KEY_ID: active encryption key version label
# SECRET AI_INTEGRATION_PREVIOUS_KEYS_JSON: prior key IDs to base64 keys during rotation
